Subject: Accept Doom II 1.666 and Heretic 1.0 as doom2-wad and heretic-wad

Walnut: the user's CD releases. Players who own the original boxed games often have these
early versions: Doom II 1.666 (the first retail release) and Heretic 1.0 (registered, episodes 1-3).
game-data-packager marked both unsuitable, so their owners could not package the games at all,
and patching them up is not supported. Modern source ports play them: dsda-doom loads both IWADs
and runs their title screens and demos (tested on the PS3 with dsda-doom 0.30.0). Both are now
the last alternative of the same file, so the same doom2-wad / heretic-wad package is built and
the newer releases are still preferred; the release shows as the tag (?1.666, ?1.0). Their
sha256 is added. Hexen 1.0 stays unsuitable: dsda-hexen refuses it ("The Hexen v1.0 IWAD is not
supported").

Forwarded: not yet (candidate for Debian)

diff --git a/data/doom2.yaml b/data/doom2.yaml
--- a/data/doom2.yaml
+++ b/data/doom2.yaml
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ wiki: Doom_II
 wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doom_II
 
 help_text: |
-  Please provide the DOOM2.WAD from Doom 2 version 1.9.
+  Please provide the DOOM2.WAD from Doom 2 version 1.9 or 1.666.
 
   Patching older versions is not currently supported. If you have
   an older version, it might be possible to patch it manually using dosbox.
@@ -91,14 +91,14 @@ files:
     - doom2.wad?psn
     - doom2.wad?tapwave_zodiac
